## Doctrine (billion-context §4)

**KEEP** (preserve verbatim): exact file paths, function names, signatures, line
numbers; exact error messages and stack traces; rationale behind key decisions; pending
questions, requests, and user instructions; repository state changes; configuration
values and endpoints.

**DROP** (verbose, dead-end, or re-derivable): verbatim tool output no longer referenced;
dead-end journeys; repetitive re-statements; content already captured in Goal / Progress;
intermediate thinking that led nowhere.

**Right to refuse:** if the new messages add nothing worth folding, you **MAY** return
the previous summary unchanged. Do not pad.

IMPORTANT: If new messages end with unanswered question or request to user, you **MUST**
add it to Critical Context (replacing any previous pending question if answered).

